# Copy to app/.env (which is gitignored) to configure a build.
#
# Expo inlines EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables into the JavaScript bundle at build
# time, so they are PUBLIC — anyone can read them out of the shipped app.
# Never put a secret here. (The Supabase anon key and the Maps browser key in
# src/config.js are already public by design; the service_role key belongs only
# in the server's own .env at the repo root.)
#
# Two gotchas, both verified against this project:
#  - Expo reads these from a .env FILE. Setting the variable only in your
#    shell before `npx expo export` does not reliably reach the bundle.
#  - Metro caches transforms. After changing a value, build with --clear
#    (`npx expo export --platform web --clear`) or the old value sticks.

# Absolute base URL of the Express API, including the /api suffix and no
# trailing slash. Use https:// for anything that isn't localhost: every request
# carries the signed-in user's Supabase access token in an Authorization
# header, and plain HTTP exposes that token to anyone on the network path.
#
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE=https://api.yourdomain.com/api
#
# Leave it unset for local development (the app then talks to
# http://<dev machine>:4000/api, which never leaves your machine or LAN), and
# leave it unset for a web deployment where the host proxies /api on the same
# domain as the site — the app defaults to <page origin>/api in that case and
# inherits the page's HTTPS automatically.
#
# Note this stays at the domain root even when the site itself is served from a
# subfolder: <origin>/api, not <origin>/<subfolder>/api. Set it explicitly if
# your proxy lives somewhere else.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Subfolder hosting (build-time only — not an EXPO_PUBLIC_ runtime value)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set this when the site is served from a subdirectory rather than the domain
# root, which is the case on Hostinger because its Git tool clones into a
# subfolder of the document root. app.config.js feeds it to Expo's
# experiments.baseUrl so the exported asset URLs carry the prefix; without it
# the page loads blank and the console shows 404s for the JS bundle.
#
# Use a plain subpath with a leading slash and no trailing slash. A value that
# isn't a valid URL subpath fails the build rather than producing a broken site.
#
#   WEB_BASE_PATH=/glp
#
# In CI this comes from the repository variable of the same name, not from here.
# Leave blank to build for the domain root.
WEB_BASE_PATH=
